{"text":"saw this boy standing in the shadow of a doorway, looking just like Sonny. I almost called his name. Then I saw that it wasn't Sonny, but somebodv we used to know, a boy from around our block. He'd been Sonnv's friend. He'd never been mine, ha\\\"ing been too young for me, and. anvwav, I'd ne\\er liked him. And now. even though he was a grown-up man. he still hung around that block, still spent hours on the street comers, wiS always high and ragg%'. I used to run into him from time to time and he'd often work around to asking me for a quarter or fift\\' cents. He always had some real good excuse, too. and I alwavs ga\\e it to him. I don't know why.\n\nBut now, abruptlv, I hated him. I couldn't stand the way he looked at me, partlv like a dog. partlv like a cunning child. I wanted to ask him what the hell he was doing in the school courtyard.\n\nHe sort of shuffled over to me, and he said, \"I see you got the papers. So you already know about it.\"\n\n\"You mean about Sonnv? Yes, I alreadv know about it. How come they didn't get you?\"\n\nHe grinned. It made him repulsive and it also brought to mind what he'd looked like as a kid. \"I wasn't there. I stay away from them people.\"\n\n\"Good for you.\" I offered him a cigarette and I watched him through the smoke. \"You come all the wav down here just to tell me about Sonnv?\"\n\n\"TTiat's right.\" He was sort of shaking his head and his eyes looked strange, as though they were about to cross. The bright sun deadened his damp dark brown skin and it made his eyes look yellow and showed up the dirt in his kinked hair. He smclled funky.3 I moved a little awav from him and I said, '^^ ell. thanks. But I already know about it and I got to get home.\"\n\n\"I'll walk you a little wavs.\" he said. We started walking. There were a couple of kids still loitering in the courtyard and one of them said goodnight to me and looked strangelv at the boy beside me.\n\n\"^^ hat're vou going to do?\" he asked me. \"I mean, about Sonny?\"\n\n\"Look. I haven't seen Sonny for over a year, I'm not sure I'm going to do anvthing. .\\nvwav. what the hell can I do?\"\n\n\"That's right,\" he said quicklv, \"ain't nothing you can do. Can't much help old Sonny no more, I guess.\"\n\nIt was what I was thinking and so it seemed to me he had no right to say it.\n\n\"I'm surprised at Sonnv, though,\" he went on—he had a funny way of talking, he looked straight ahead as though he were talking to himself—\"I thought Sonny was a smart boy, I thought he was too smart to get hung.\"\n\n\"I guess he thought so too.\" I said sharply, \"and that's how he got hung. And how about you? You're pretty goddamn smart, I bet.\"","voice":"en-US-AriaNeural","words":[[0.1,0.3875,0,3],[0.4,0.65,4,8],[0.6625,0.8875,9,12],[0.9,1.375,13,21],[1.3875,1.4625,22,24],[1.475,1.5375,25,28],[1.55,1.975,29,35],[1.9875,2.05,36,38],[2.0625,2.1375,39,40],[2.15,2.625,41,48],[2.9375,3.225,50,57],[3.2375,3.5125,58,62],[3.525,3.7,63,67],[3.7125,4.175,68,73],[5.05,5.225,75,76],[5.2375,5.65,77,83],[5.6625,5.9,84,90],[5.9125,6.05,91,94],[6.0625,6.4875,95,99],[7.3625,7.6125,101,105],[7.625,7.7125,106,107],[7.725,7.9625,108,111],[7.975,8.1,112,116],[8.1125,8.1875,117,119],[8.2,8.55,120,126],[8.5625,8.9,127,132],[9.15,9.3125,134,137],[9.325,9.775,138,146],[9.7875,9.9,147,149],[9.9125,10.15,150,154],[10.1625,10.2375,155,157],[10.25,10.6,158,162],[10.775,10.8375,164,165],[10.85,11.075,166,169],[11.0875,11.25,170,174],[11.2625,11.6375,175,181],[11.65,11.7625,182,185],[11.775,12.2625,186,191],[13.125,13.35,193,197],[13.3625,13.5625,198,202],[13.575,13.9375,203,210],[13.95,14.4125,211,217],[15.275,15.5125,219,223],[15.525,15.8125,224,229],[15.825,15.9875,230,234],[16.0,16.3875,235,239],[16.6125,16.7375,241,243],[17.4,17.9,245,248],[17.9125,18.075,249,253],[18.0875,18.275,254,257],[18.2875,18.55,258,263],[18.5625,18.7,264,267],[18.7125,18.95,268,270],[19.1625,19.6,272,275],[20.4625,21.025,277,283],[21.1875,21.3625,285,288],[21.375,21.525,289,291],[22.175,